+### The Python file (!57 to !60)
+
+!57 added `Assets/Python/EntryPoints/CvGameInterface.py` to the mod so that the DLL could ask
+Python for the camera. Its commit calls it the Beyond the Sword file unchanged, but it is not:
+- it defines 49 functions besides the camera's, and its `gameUtils()` returns a plain
+  `CvGameUtils.CvGameUtils()`;
+- it never imports `CvGameInterfaceFile`. The mod ships BUG's `CvGameInterfaceFile.py`, which
+  "overrides the use of CvGameUtils with BUG's modular game utils dispatcher";
+- Firaxis's own DLL source (the BTS SDK in this repository) calls 22 `CvGameInterface` functions it
+  lacks. Among them are `getUnitCostMod`, `getBuildingCostMod`, `getUpgradePriceOverride`,
+  `getExperienceNeeded`, `doPillageGold`, `doCityCaptureGold`, `getExtraCost`, `canBuild` and
+  `cannotFoundCity`.
+
+A mod's file replaces the game's file of the same name. RoM's rules in `RoMGameUtils.py`, which
+`Assets/Config/RoMSettings.xml` registers through BUG's dispatcher, were therefore not reached:
+- `cannotConstruct` and `cannotDoCivic` went to the plain game utils;
+- `getUnitCostMod`, `getBuildingCostMod`, `getUpgradePriceOverride`, `doPillageGold` and
+  `doCityCaptureGold` were not found at all.
+
+The cost, upgrade-price, cannot-construct and cannot-do-civic switches are on in
+`PythonCallbackDefines.xml`. `getExperienceNeeded` has no switch. What the game does when it calls
+a missing function is not known.
+
+`claude/paging-interface` moves `getCameraView`, unchanged, to the mod's `CvScreensInterface.py`
+(`PYScreensModule`, which the DLL already calls). It deletes the mod's `CvGameInterface.py`, so the
+game's own file answers again. With the DLL of !60 and the new Python, the camera cannot be read
+and the fixed window is used, as before !60.
 
